WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.600
It's that time of year when your favorite
series are back — like This Is Us, The Good

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.950
Place, Better Things, and even Will &amp; Grace.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:10.910
But there are also a number of brand new network
and on-demand shows that are sure to blow

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:11.929
you away.

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:16.219
Here's a rundown of the shows that premiered
in Fall of 2017 that you should definitely

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:18.130
make some time for.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.420
The Mayor

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.670
The time is right for a new political comedy
to step up and help us temporarily escape

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:27.660
from real-life drama — and ABC's The Mayor
is here to help.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.880
Centering around the charismatic Brandon Michael
Hall's character Courtney Rose — an aspiring

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.159
rapper who gets elected mayor after running
for office as a publicity stunt — The Mayor

00:00:36.159 --> 00:00:39.600
could potentially be crowned this season's
best new comedy.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.280
It's funny, refreshingly light-hearted, and
optimistic — and it certainly has our vote

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.980
of confidence.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.260
Future Man

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:50.949
If Seth Rogen is releasing a project, it should
probably be on your radar.

00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:55.289
The well-established funnyman is once again
teaming up with Evan Goldberg to take on the

00:00:55.289 --> 00:00:59.480
end of the world — a favorite topic of the
two This is The End creators.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:04.190
With their show Future Man, Rogen and Goldberg
are looking to stand out from the comedy crowd

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:06.360
with their own patented brand of humor.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:11.440
In an interview with SYFY Wire, Rogen and
Goldberg said that they prefer very high-stakes

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.530
comedy...and Future Man is exactly that.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.740
"People could die at any second.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.270
To us, that's the funniest.

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:20.500
I don't know why, probably because we're sick."

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.250
Star Trek: Discovery

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:26.730
As the first new Star Trek show in more than
a decade, Star Trek: Discovery is under some

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.810
serious pressure to perform.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:32.920
Setting the expectations even higher is the
fact that it takes place after Star Trek:

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:38.660
Enterprise and before the original series
of the 1960s, meaning Discovery needs to successfully

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:42.970
maintain continuity if it wants to please
the franchise's hardcore fanbase.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:47.730
Luckily, fans have tweeted out their positive
reactions, so perhaps all systems are, indeed,

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:48.730
a go.

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:53.180
With the charismatic Sonequa Martin-Green
headlining a cast of almost all new characters,

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.450
Discovery should please longtime Trekkies
and newcomers alike.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.710
SMILF

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:03.640
Showtime's hottest new series this fall is
undoubtedly SMILF, about a basketball-playing,

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:08.420
man-chasing South Boston woman who also happens
to be a single mother raising a toddler.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:13.880
SMILF thrives in its authentic feel, thanks
to writer, producer, director and star Frankie

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.280
Shaw, who claims the show is semi-autobiographical.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.300
With Rosie O'Donnell as Shaw's mother and
Nashville's Connie Britton on board, it looks

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.450
like Showtime is set to score a big win with
SMILF.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:26.450
Big Mouth

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:32.120
If adult-themed animated comedies are your
thing, look no further than Netflix's definitely-not-family-friendly

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:37.170
series Big Mouth, which follows two teenagers
in the throes of puberty as they battle hormone

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.340
monsters and newfound adolescent interests.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.260
Throw in a star-studded cast — featuring
comedy favorites like Nick Kroll, Maya Rudolph,

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.640
John Mulaney, and Jordan Peele, to name a
few — and the fact that Netflix has already

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:54.990
proven itself with adult animated shows, and
Big Mouth is sure to be a home run.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.900
"You have a really big mouth"

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.990
"Thank you, I think?"

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:02.990
The Deuce

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:04.790
Can't get enough of James Franco?

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:09.670
Then HBO's new series The Deuce is for you
— featuring the actor in not one but two

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:14.680
leading roles, while also working behind the
scenes as an executive producer and director.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:19.410
The drama follows twin brothers Vincent and
Frankie Martino, both played by Franco, during

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.590
the early days of New York City's porn industry.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:26.060
The creators of the series have already laid
out their plan of exactly how they want it

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.780
to go, with eight episodes per season for
three seasons.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.880
In an interview with Collider, Franco said,

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:37.120
"I think if we pull it off, it will be a really
nice encapsulation of a time and a place."

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.120
Young Sheldon

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:43.920
CBS's ultra-popular sitcom The Big Bang Theory
was destined to get a spinoff — and here

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:44.920
it is.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:49.099
Young Sheldon centers around child genius
Sheldon Cooper, but the similarities stop

00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:50.099
there.

00:03:50.099 --> 00:03:54.030
Unlike its parent sitcom, Young Sheldon has
no studio audience, and it has a more sentimental,

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.030
family-oriented tone.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:58.400
"How can I be excited when he's gonna be in
the same grade as me?"

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.430
"Don't worry Georgie I'm not planning on being
in the 9th grade for very long."

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:07.100
This stylistic change in format works in the
spinoff's favor, as does the standout work

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.660
of Iain Armitage as the title character.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:13.099
Whether you're a fan of The Big Bang Theory
or not, you'll definitely want to give the

00:04:13.099 --> 00:04:16.150
more mature Young Sheldon a chance.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.150
Lore

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:22.100
Based on Aaron Mahnke's popular podcast of
the same name, Amazon's Lore is set to dominate

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.900
the horror genre this season.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:28.500
The series' first season will run for six
episodes, with each episode acting as a standalone

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.820
horror story, running the gamut from demons
to medical experiments gone wrong.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.990
If frights are your thing, be sure to check
out Lore.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.690
American Vandal

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:42.350
Whether you love or hate true crime documentaries,
you'll certainly get a kick out of Netflix's

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.750
self-satirizing spoof American Vandal.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:49.400
The series lampoons the all-too-familiar genre
by focusing on the crime and punishment of

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:54.400
Dylan Maxwell, a high schooler expelled for
drawing male genitalia across 27 automobiles.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.360
"Because everyone thinks I did it."

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.360
"Did what?"

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.360
"The d----"

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:04.590
What ensues is an utterly brilliant deconstruction
of everyone's favorite binge-worthy guilty

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:07.930
pleasure…and it's one you definitely won't
want to miss.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.270
The Gifted

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:13.450
Marvel series are always met with anticipation,
and The Gifted is no different.

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:17.370
So far, fans and critics agree — it's definitely
delivering.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:21.430
The Gifted excels in both its premise — a
mutant family on the run from the Sentinel

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:25.090
Services — and the special effects it uses
for its mutants' powers.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:29.680
Whether you're an X-men fan or not, The Gifted's
impressive cast will — quite literally — blow

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.169
you away.

00:05:31.169 --> 00:05:32.169
Thanks for watching!

00:05:32.169 --> 00:05:34.780
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.980
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

